-- title:
--   Translation preserves openness
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a real inner product space and, for $S \subseteq E$ and $x \in E$, write
--   $$S[x] \;=\; S + x \;=\; \{y \in E : y - x \in S\}$$
--   for the translate of $S$ by $x$. If $S$ is open then $S[x]$ is open.
--
--   Translation is a homeomorphism of $E$, and this is the instance of that fact used throughout: cones, cubes and balls are defined at the origin and then moved to an arbitrary base point, and every topological property must travel with them.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The statement holds for an arbitrary real inner product space $E$; no hypothesis is placed on $x$.
